<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Court of Justice of the European Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1952">1952</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as CJEU, European Court of Justice</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Court of Justice of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a> is the judicial institution of the European Union, seated in Luxembourg. It began in 1952 as the Court of Justice of the European <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">Coal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">Steel</a> Community and became the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-communities">European Communities</a>. It interprets EU law and ensures its uniform application, and its rulings, notably on the direct effect and primacy of Community law in the 1960s, shaped the European legal order.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/court-of-justice-of-the-european-union.jpg" alt="Court of Justice of the European Union" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FDRMRZUSA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Official_Emblem_of_the_Court_of_Justice_of_the_European_Union.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
